WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.427 --> 00:00:14.150
you don't behave," I said to the boy, "I'll take you straight home.

2
00:00:14.810 --> 00:00:16.892
Now are you going to be good or not?"

3
00:00:17.912 --> 00:00:20.814
"I was just having a little fun," he said with a pout.

4
00:00:20.834 --> 00:00:23.196
"I didn't mean to hurt Old Hank.

5
00:00:23.636 --> 00:00:25.017
But what did he hit me for?

6
00:00:25.878 --> 00:00:28.640
I'll behave, Snake-eye, if you don't send me home.

7
00:00:29.568 --> 00:00:32.689
And I'll be really good if you'll let me play the Black Scout today."

8
00:00:32.709 --> 00:00:35.050
"I don't know that game," I said.

9
00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:36.351
"That's for you and Mr.

10
00:00:36.371 --> 00:00:37.191
Bill to decide.

11
00:00:37.571 --> 00:00:38.972
He's your playmate for the day.

12
00:00:39.972 --> 00:00:41.993
I'm going away for a while, on business.

13
00:00:42.514 --> 00:00:44.434
Now you make friends with Bill right now.

14
00:00:45.335 --> 00:00:48.376
Say you're sorry for hurting him, or you'll go home at once."

15
00:00:49.396 --> 00:00:53.458
Red Chief shook hands with Bill, and then I took my friend outside the cave so we could

16
00:00:53.498 --> 00:00:57.480
talk. "The village of Poplar Cove is three miles from here.

17
00:00:58.420 --> 00:01:01.743
I'm going to find out if they've heard anything about the kidnapping," I said.

18
00:01:01.763 --> 00:01:06.868
"Also I think it's best if we send old man Dorset a ransom letter today.

19
00:01:07.448 --> 00:01:09.690
We'll demand the money and tell him how to deliver it."

20
00:01:10.551 --> 00:01:15.656
"You know, Sam," Bill said, "I've stood by you during earthquakes without batting an eye.

21
00:01:16.817 --> 00:01:19.919
In fire and flood, I've been shoulder to shoulder with you.

22
00:01:21.020 --> 00:01:24.884
In poker games, police raids, train robberies, and cyclones!

23
00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:30.524
I never lost my nerve until we kidnapped that two-legged skyrocket of a kid.

24
00:01:31.385 --> 00:01:34.147
You won't leave me with him a long time, will you, Sam?"

25
00:01:35.108 --> 00:01:37.150
"I'll be back this afternoon," I said.

26
00:01:37.170 --> 00:01:39.972
"Keep the boy amused until I return.

27
00:01:40.132 --> 00:01:41.894
I won't be long, I promise.

28
00:01:42.634 --> 00:01:44.876
Now let's write the letter to old Dorset."

29
00:01:46.057 --> 00:01:50.381
Bill and I got paper and pencil and worked on the letter while Red Chief, with a blanket

30
00:01:50.421 --> 00:01:53.944
wrapped around him, strutted up and down, guarding the mouth of the cave.

31
00:01:55.112 --> 00:02:00.396
"Make the ransom fifteen hundred dollars instead of two thousand," Bill begged with tears in his eyes.

32
00:02:00.416 --> 00:02:06.280
"I'm not questioning a parent's love for a child, but we're dealing with human beings here.

33
00:02:07.341 --> 00:02:13.225
Nobody is going to give up two thousand dollars for that forty-pound devil, that freckled wildcat.

34
00:02:14.166 --> 00:02:17.208
Please, Sam, let's just ask for fifteen hundred dollars."

35
00:02:18.148 --> 00:02:20.150
To make Bill happy, I agreed.

36
00:02:20.590 --> 00:02:24.453
We worked together on a letter that read like this: Dear Mr.

37
00:02:24.553 --> 00:02:29.056
Ebenezer Dorset: We have your boy hidden in a place far from Summit.

38
00:02:29.916 --> 00:02:33.819
It is useless for you or the most skillful detectives to attempt to find him.

39
00:02:34.659 --> 00:02:41.744
We will only return him if these conditions are met: we demand fifteen hundred dollars in large bills.

40
00:02:42.885 --> 00:02:48.849
If you agree to these conditions, send your answer by a lone messenger tonight at half-past eight o'clock.

41
00:02:49.790 --> 00:02:55.942
After crossing Owl Creek, and on the road to Poplar Cove, there are three large trees about a

42
00:02:56.022 --> 00:03:01.005
hundred yards apart, close to a fence bordering a wheat field on the right-hand side.

43
00:03:02.246 --> 00:03:07.430
At the bottom of the fence post opposite the third tree, there is a small cardboard box.

44
00:03:08.470 --> 00:03:13.654
Your messenger will place your answer and the money in this box and return immediately to Summit.

45
00:03:14.955 --> 00:03:21.720
If you attempt any tricks, or fail to follow our instructions, you will never see your boy again.

46
00:03:22.980 --> 00:03:27.501
If you pay the money, he will be returned safe and well within three hours.

47
00:03:28.402 --> 00:03:29.902
These conditions are final.

48
00:03:30.882 --> 00:03:34.884
If you do not accept them, no further communication will be attempted.

49
00:03:35.764 --> 00:03:40.385
TWO DESPERATE MEN I addressed the letter to Dorset, and put it in my pocket.

50
00:03:41.346 --> 00:03:43.426
As I was about to leave, the kid came up to me.

51
00:03:43.446 --> 00:03:49.128
"Aw, Snake-eye, you said I could play the Black Scout while you were gone," the boy said.

52
00:03:50.276 --> 00:03:51.676
"Play it, of course," I said.

53
00:03:51.696 --> 00:03:53.197
"Mr. Bill will play with you.

54
00:03:53.277 --> 00:03:54.557
What kind of a game is it?"

55
00:03:55.678 --> 00:03:59.879
"I'm the Black Scout," Red Chief said, "and I have to ride to the fort to warn the

56
00:03:59.939 --> 00:04:01.399
settlers that the Indians are coming.

57
00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:04.700
I'm tired of playing Indian by myself.

58
00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:06.661
I want to be the Black Scout."

59
00:04:06.681 --> 00:04:08.541
"All right," I said.

60
00:04:08.561 --> 00:04:10.022
"It sounds harmless to me.

61
00:04:10.422 --> 00:04:11.462
Mr. Bill will help you."

62
00:04:11.482 --> 00:04:13.503
"What do I have to do?"

63
00:04:13.863 --> 00:04:15.043
Bill asked suspiciously.

64
00:04:15.063 --> 00:04:17.844
"You are the horse," Black Scout said.

65
00:04:18.732 --> 00:04:20.393
"Get down on your hands and knees.

66
00:04:20.773 --> 00:04:22.833
How can I ride to the fort without a horse?"

67
00:04:23.693 --> 00:04:27.735
"You better keep him interested, Bill," I said, "until we get this scheme going.

68
00:04:28.195 --> 00:04:28.755
Loosen up."

69
00:04:29.855 --> 00:04:34.377
Bill got down on all fours, and a look came into his eyes like a rabbit gets when

70
00:04:34.417 --> 00:04:35.397
it's caught in a trap.

71
00:04:36.337 --> 00:04:38.198
"How far is it to the fort, kid?"

72
00:04:38.598 --> 00:04:39.258
he croaked.

73
00:04:40.538 --> 00:04:46.140
"Ninety miles," the Black Scout said, "and you have to gallop hard to get there on time."

74
00:04:47.212 --> 00:04:50.696
The Black Scout jumped on Bill's back and dug his heels into his sides.

75
00:04:50.716 --> 00:04:55.921
"For heaven's sake, Sam," Bill said, "hurry back as soon as you can.

76
00:04:57.182 --> 00:05:00.065
I wish we hadn't made the ransom more than a thousand."

77
00:05:01.006 --> 00:05:06.411
Then Bill turned to Red Chief—excuse me—Black Scout, who was still sitting on his back.

78
00:05:06.431 --> 00:05:11.216
"Quit kicking me," shouted Bill, "or I'll get up and spank you hard!"

79
00:05:12.264 --> 00:05:17.006
I walked over to Poplar Cove and sat around the post office and store, talking with the country

80
00:05:17.046 --> 00:05:17.886
hicks that came in.

81
00:05:19.067 --> 00:05:28.551
One old farmer said, "I hear Summit is all upset about Ebenezer Dorset's boy being lost or stolen."

82
00:05:28.571 --> 00:05:31.252
"What great news!"

83
00:05:31.332 --> 00:05:33.073
I thought as I bought some soda.

84
00:05:34.093 --> 00:05:39.775
To look casual, I remarked to no one in particular, "The price of black-eyed peas seems a bit

85
00:05:39.835 --> 00:05:41.056
high this season."

86
00:05:42.228 --> 00:05:45.390
Then I dropped my letter into the mail slot when no one was looking.

87
00:05:46.291 --> 00:05:51.213
As I walked away, I overheard the postmaster telling a customer that the mail would go out to

88
00:05:51.274 --> 00:05:52.474
Summit in one hour.

89
00:05:53.355 --> 00:05:56.236
When I got back to the cave, I could not find Bill and the boy.

90
00:05:57.177 --> 00:06:02.380
I explored the entire cave and the surrounding area and risked a yodel or two, but there was

91
00:06:02.520 --> 00:06:03.261
no response.

92
00:06:04.441 --> 00:06:08.544
So I lit my pipe and sat down on a mossy bank to see what would happen next.
